WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Hydrogen becomes helium inside the core. At the

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.760
same mass density and temperature, this means fewer

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.840
pressure bearing particles. The core slowly contracts and

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.360
heats. Hydrogen fusion speeds up, so the main

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.000
sequence Sun gradually becomes more luminous.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.400
After core hydrogen is exhausted, the helium core

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.600
contracts while hydrogen burns around it in a

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.240
shell. The envelope expands and its surface cools.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.260
The hot core and cool outer surface are

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.460
different regions. This is a coupled structural response,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.860
not a claim that every layer moves together.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.540
In the supplied low mass model, helium ignites

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.460
rapidly inside the core. This helium flash is

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.980
not a visible supernova. The core then expands

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.600
somewhat, the envelope shrinks and warms, and total

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.320
luminosity falls. On the H R diagram, that

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.860
change moves down and left.
